+- Step 4 costing and quotation (19.0.1.2.0), built from the client's own quoting process (their costing sheets), not from
+  DynamicsPrint. Principle: what belongs to one job is typed on the estimate; Configuration holds only what is reused.
+  - Labels in plain words: Copies ordered (run_qty), Extra copies, Extra sheets, Press %. One "Production" tab
+    (parts + finishing), a "Costing" tab, and "Calculated" (the old Print overview, read-only).
+  - print.estimate.page._plan(qty, spine) is PURE (reads, writes nothing) and is the single source of geometry,
+    quantities and part costs; _calculate() stores it for the copies ordered. Quantity breaks call _plan() only.
+  - Typed overrides per part: ups, plates, per_parent (pages or pieces per paper sheet as bought), plate_rate, print_rate.
+    Each has a *_typed flag. The same field shows the calculated value; typing wins; 0 on a count = back to calculated;
+    unticking the flag on a rate = back to standard. Every override is in the calculation log and in override_note.
+  - A part with typed ups AND typed per_parent needs no press (the sheet's way of working). Press % always needs a press.
+  - Standard plate rate and printing rate (per plate per 1,000 impressions, minimum 1,000) are dated fields on
+    print.workcenter.rate. Thousands = impressions per plate WITHOUT waste / 1,000, rounded up, minimum 1.
+  - print.operation (+ dated print.operation.rate with minimum charge): lamination, binding, die cutting, making, packing,
+    delivery ... costed per piece, per 1,000, per sq ft, per sq in, per hour or fixed. Names are seeded, rates are not.
+  - print.estimate.operation: count follows copies ordered until typed (typed count scales with other quantities),
+    extra qty is never changed by the app, piece W x H for area work.
+  - print.estimate.cost.line: the costing sheet, rebuilt by every calculation, with a "how" text on every line.
+  - Price: (subtotal + overheads %) / copies = cost per copy; + margin % on cost = price per copy; a typed price wins.
+    Defaults for overheads, margin, tax, validity days and terms are system parameters (Settings), never constants.
+  - print.estimate.qty: other quantities, each planned and costed in full; extra copies / sheets stay fixed.
+  - Every gap (no paper price, no rate, no piece size, part error) is a warning that makes the costing incomplete.
+    Incomplete = cannot be marked quoted unless a manager accepts it with a reason; a new gap cancels the acceptance;
+    the quotation prints with an INTERNAL watermark until complete or accepted.
+  - Quotation PDF (report/quote_report.xml): specification and price per quantity, never costs.
+  - Configuration > Costing > Load sample job: the Model Town sheet as a worked example (records named SAMPLE).
+  - Regression checks from the costing sheets (tests/test_costing.py): Model Town 350 copies = 428.80 per copy
+    (subtotal 140,262.87 with lamination on 350 + 150 extra pieces); Zameen 4,000 copies = 224.89 per copy.
+- pp_print_sale (19.0.1.0.0, depends pp_print_core + sale): "Create sales order" on a quoted estimate makes one draft
+  sale.order with one line (service product "Print job", quantity = copies ordered, price = price per copy, the
+  specification as the description). No stored field on sale.order. Install it once from Apps.
