+## Step 4: costing and quotation
+Built from the client's own quoting process. What belongs to a job is typed on the estimate.
+
+**Production tab**
+- Header: copies ordered, extra copies (fills each new part), format, W x H in inches with mm beside it.
+- Printed parts, one row each: part, pages, colours front / back, paper (create one on the spot with its first price),
+  ups, per parent sheet, plates, extra qty with its unit (copies / sheets / press %), plate rate, printing rate,
+  paper sheets and paper cost, "changed from standard".
+  - Ups, per parent sheet and plates show the calculated value. Type your own number to override; type 0 to go back.
+  - Plate and printing rates show the standard of the press on the estimate date. A typed rate wins; untick
+    "typed" (optional column) to go back.
+  - With ups and per parent sheet both typed, a part needs no press.
+- Finishing and other work: operation, count (follows copies ordered until typed), extra qty, piece size for area
+  work, rate, amount.
+
+**Costing tab**
+- The costing sheet: one line per paper, plates, printing and finishing line, each with how it is calculated.
+- Overheads %, margin % (on cost), typed price per copy (0 = calculated), sales tax %.
+- Other quantities to quote: each is planned and costed in full.
+- If something is missing (a price, a rate, a piece size) the costing is incomplete: it cannot be marked as quoted
+  until it is filled in or a manager accepts it with a reason.
+
+**Buttons**: Mark as quoted, Print quotation, Order confirmed (or Create sales order with `pp_print_sale`).
+
+**Configuration**
+- Production > Work centres > Rates: plate rate and printing rate per plate per 1,000 for each press (dated).
+- Costing > Finishing and other operations: how each is costed and its dated rates. Names are seeded, rates are not.
+- Settings > Costing and quotation: default overheads, margin, sales tax, validity days and terms.
+- Costing > Load sample job: creates "SAMPLE Magazine 14K Model Town" (350 copies, 428.80 per copy) to check the screens.
+
+**Formulas**
+- Paper sheets = print sheets with extra / print sheets per paper sheet; cost = sheets x cost per sheet (by weight).
+- Plates = printed sides x colours (or typed). Printing = plates x thousands x rate; thousands = impressions per plate
+  without waste / 1,000, rounded up, minimum 1.
+- Area work = (count + extra) x W x H / 144 sq ft x rate.
+- Price per copy = (subtotal + overheads) / copies x (1 + margin).
+
+Tested on Odoo 19: 25 unit tests in this module, 1 in `pp_print_sale` (`--test-tags=pp_print_core`), including the
+client's Model Town (428.80) and Zameen (224.89) sheets, and an upgrade from 19.0.1.1.1 with existing estimates.
+
 ## Rules followed in every step
 - Every rate, price, speed, markup and allowance is a record, never a constant in code.
 - Rates and prices are effective-dated; an estimate will use the rates valid on its date.
