+- Step 5 job ticket (pp_print_core 19.0.1.3.0): Estimate (confirmed order) > "Create job ticket" makes ONE live print.job
+  (a cancelled job does not count; it can be remade). The job is a SNAPSHOT of the estimate: print.job.part (paper to issue,
+  planned paper cost) and print.job.step (plates and printing per part, then each finishing line, with planned qty and cost).
+  Later edits of the estimate never change a released job.
+  - Real work: start / finish / skip per step; good and waste qty; machine hours (x work-centre direct + indirect rate on
+    the release date); outside cost; paper really issued per part (x the estimate's cost per sheet).
+  - Person-wise time: print.worker (shop-floor people, not Odoo users) + print.job.time. The role rate valid on the work date
+    is saved on the entry, so a later rate change never changes old entries.
+  - "Estimate against actual" tab: planned (estimate subtotal, before overheads) against actual paper + work. Overheads on
+    neither side.
+  - Job ticket PDF (report/job_report.xml): parts, paper to issue, route with blank Good / Waste / Done-by columns.
+  - Stock is NOT moved yet: "paper issued" is a typed number. Real stock moves come with the stock/purchasing step.
