+## Step 5: job ticket
+- On a confirmed estimate press **Create job ticket**. The job copies the plan: parts with the paper to issue, and a route of
+  steps (plates and printing for each part, then the finishing lines). Release it to production.
+- Per step: start, finish, skip; good and waste quantity, machine hours, outside cost, and who worked (Time tab: worker,
+  hours; the cost uses the worker's role rate on that date).
+- Per part: type the paper sheets really issued.
+- "Estimate against actual" shows planned against actual cost, before overheads.
+- **Print job ticket** gives the shop-floor sheet with blank Good / Waste / Done-by columns.
+- Configuration > Production > Workers: the people whose time is logged (they do not need an Odoo login).
+- A released job does not change when the estimate is edited.
+
 ## Rules followed in every step
 - Every rate, price, speed, markup and allowance is a record, never a constant in code.
 - Rates and prices are effective-dated; an estimate will use the rates valid on its date.
